      "contentPreview": "CORRECTS AN EARLIER LEDGER CLAIM \u2014 read before scoping any NMP/2 work. HttpMemoryStore.cs:921-924 hand-rolls a per-chunk decode loop. Two things previously recorded about it are FALSE: (1) it does NOT decode a remote server response \u2014 the artifact comes from GetEphemeral -\u003E _ephemeral, a process-local ConcurrentDictionary written only from inside HttpMemoryStore with locally-encoded content, so there is no untrusted input on that path; (2) the in-code comment at HttpMemoryStore.cs:919 claiming t",
